{
  "title": "Wartenberg's Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6025/wartenbergs-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 18 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Wartenberg's Syndrome, also called \"cheiralgia paresthetica,\" is a compressive neuropathy of the superficial sensory radial nerve at the wrist.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with pain and paresthesias over the dorsoradial hand without any motor deficits.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is conservative with rest, wrist splints and CSIs with surgical decompression reserved for refractory cases.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "< 1 per 100,000 annually",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male:female ratio is 1:4, more common in **women**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age bracket is **20-70 years**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "SRN compressed by scissoring action of **brachioradialis** and **ECRL tendons** during **forearm pronation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6025/images/scissor.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "also by **fascial bands** at its exit site in the subcutaneous plane",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with De Quervain's disease in 20-50%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The superficial sensory branch of the radial nerve",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6025/images/Hoppenfield%205_moved.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arises from the bifurcation of the radial nerve in the proximal forearm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "travels deep to the **brachioradialis** in the forearm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "emerges from between **brachioradialis** and **ECRL** 9 cm proximal to radial styloid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bifurcates proximal to the wrist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dorsal branch lies 1-3cm radial to Lister's tubercle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "supplies 1st and 2nd web space",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "palmar branch passes within 2cm of 1st dorsal compartment, directly over EPL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "supplies dorsolateral thumb",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may have history of trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "forearm fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**handcuffs**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tight wrist band, wristwatch band, bracelet or plaster cast",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ill-defined pain over dorsoradial hand** (does not like to wear watch)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**paresthesias over dorsoradial hand**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**numbness**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptom aggravation by motions involving **repetitive wrist flexion and ulnar deviation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "no motor weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Tinel's sign** over the superficial sensory radial nerve (most common exam finding)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**wrist flexion, ulnar deviation and pronation** for one minute",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6025/images/flexion.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Finkelstein test** increases symptoms in 96% of patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "because of traction on the nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "of limited value",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may demonstrate old forearm fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Electrodiagnostic tests",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "EMG and NCV of limited value",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnostic injection",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**diagnostic wrist block** may temporarily relieve pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**De Quervain's tenosynovitis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain is not aggravated by wrist pronation, unlike Wartenberg Syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve (LACN) neuritis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "positive Tinel's sign over LACN can be mistaken for positive Tinel's over superficial sensory radial nerve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Intersection syndrome**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may have dorsoradial forearm swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptom exacerbation and \"wet leather\" crepitus on repeated wrist flexion/extension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diagnosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Clinical",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis is made with careful history and physical examination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, activity modification, NSAIDS, and wrist splints",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "avoid aggravating activities",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "remove inciting factors (e.g. tight wristwatch band)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "corticosteroid injection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "although evidence to support this is limited",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical decompression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms persist after 6 months",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Surgical Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Surgical Decompression**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "longitudinal incision **volar** to Tinel's sign",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "to avoid injury to LACN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "to avoid tethering of incision scar over SRN",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "decompression technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**neurolysis** and release of **fascia** between brachioradialis and ECRL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Failed decompression**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Persistent pain and numbness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Wound dehiscence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Spontaneous resolution** of symptoms is common",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment outcomes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "74% success after surgical decompression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
